---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Methodology" description="How a spec cell is marked verified, and which cells are refused." crumbs={[{ name: "Home", href: "/" }, { name: "Methodology", href: "/methodology/" }]}>
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <p>
    A status that begins with VERIFIED is rendered. Any other status is omitted, except a conflict status, which is shown as a conflict and not as a chosen number.
    The template does not average two documents and does not invent a missing loader model.
  </p>
  <p>
    Horsepower pairs are kept as printed. Mechanical horsepower and metric PS are not treated as the same unit.
    The 4066M gear cell prints 58 (53.2). That pair does not match either conversion, so the page says so.
    The Kubota L2502 has two published PTO pairs. Both stay.
  </p>
  <p>
    Hitch phrases are not normalized. Limited Category 1 is not stored as Category 1.
    Lift numbers keep the measurement point when the document names one.
  </p>
  <p>
    Dealer-hosted John Deere files are labeled as dealer-hosted. Filter numbers come from Deere or Kubota documents, not from a third-party cross-reference chart.
  </p>
</Base>
